            <div xml:id="d978">

                <pb facs="0996" n="984" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.0011B/5</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Woodring</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-17">May 17, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged
                    of your letter of May 12, 1937, in which the comments of the War Department are
                        <pb facs="0997" n="985" xml:id="pg985"/> requested with regard to a
                    memorandum which it is proposed to send to certain diplomatic missions in
                    Washington on the subject of the relations between foreign consuls in the
                    Philippine Islands and the Commonwealth Government of the Philippines.</p>
                <p>I am pleased to inform you that this Department concurs in the memorandum as
                    drafted.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry H. Woodring</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
